{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/57508","id":4565883964,"node_id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABECXcPA","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57508","diff_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57508.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57508.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/57508","number":57508,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Bugfix][Model] Fix MiMo-V2.5 fused fp8 qkv_proj sharding (pre-shard count is num_key_value_heads; MTP path too)","user":{"login":"vllmellm","id":190700713,"node_id":"U_kgDOC13cqQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190700713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm","html_url":"https://github.com/vllmellm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vllmellm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Purpose\r\n\r\n`XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5` cannot load on current main at any TP size. \r\n\r\nCurrently with TP4, on mi355x/mi300x we will hit this error.\r\n\r\n```\r\nFile \".../vllm/model_executor/models/mimo_v2.py\", line 527, in _shard_fp8_qkv_proj\r\n    w_g_dequant = w_g * s_g_expanded\r\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (1856) must match the size of tensor b (1792) at non-singleton dimension 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is not platform specific, so every platform that runs this checkpoint is affected.\r\n\r\nThe root cause is, the checkpoint's fused `qkv_proj` is pre-sharded at `ckpt_tp = config.num_key_value_heads` (4 here), each chunk holding `[Q_c | K_c | V_c]` with its own fp8 block scales, while `_shard_fp8_qkv_proj` (#45200) assumes one chunk per KV head. The assumption holds for Pro (8 KV heads / 8 chunks) and for V2.5's GA layers (4/4) — those load fine today — but not for the SWA layers: 8 KV heads over 4 chunks, so each chunk carries two KV heads.\r\n\r\nConcretely, for `model.layers.1.self_attn.qkv_proj`:\r\n- weight `(14848, 4096)` = 4 chunks of 3072 Q + 384 K + 256 V = **3712** rows = **29** blocks exactly\r\n- `weight_scale_inv` `(116, 32)` = **4 × 29**; the one-per-KV-head reading expects 8 × 15 = 120 and per-group-floor 112, so the loader's `116 // 8 = 14` expands to 1792 rows vs the 1856-row slice\r\n\r\nFor GA layers (`(13568, 108)`, chunks of 3392 = 3072+192+128) and Pro (`(27136, 216)`, 8 chunks of 3392) the pre-shard count happens to equal the KV-head count, which is why SWA breaks. \r\n\r\n## Change\r\n\r\n1. `_shard_fp8_qkv_proj` takes `ckpt_tp` (= `config.num_key_value_heads`, i.e. the number of ranks the checkpoint was pre-sharded into — 4 for MiMo-V2.5, 8 for Pro) and derives the chunk geometry from the layer's own heads/dims.\r\n   - `tp_size == ckpt_tp` → plain chunk of weight and scales (the chunk already is `[Q_r|K_r|V_r]`; scale rows line up with `ceil(rows/128)`);\r\n   - otherwise gather each rank's Q/K/V head rows from the chunks that hold them, dequantize with the per-chunk scale mapping `(row // rows_per_chunk) * ceil(rows_per_chunk/128) + (row % rows_per_chunk) // 128`, reorder and requantize (zero-padding the 26.5-block tail, since `scaled_quantize` needs full blocks);\r\n   - a scale tensor matching neither the per-chunk nor a continuous grid now raises instead of being dequantized with the wrong scale.\r\n2. TP > `num_kv_heads` (GA layers at TP=8) via KV replication, the same convention `QKVParallelLinear` uses for split checkpoints: rank *r* owns KV head `r // (tp_size // num_kv_heads)`, so each Q head stays with the KV head it attends to.\r\n3. `mimo_v2_mtp.py`: the MTP draft loader sharded the fused qkv with a plain `chunk(tp_size)` for weight *and* scales. At TP=4 that is correct by coincidence, at TP=8 the scale chunks come out `[15]*7 + [11]` against a 15-row parameter (rank 7 asserts in `default_weight_loader`) and mid-block ranks take a neighbouring block's scale. It now buffers weight + `weight_scale_inv` per layer and shards them through `_shard_fp8_qkv_proj` with `ckpt_tp = config.num_key_value_heads`; non-fp8 fused checkpoints keep the old path.\r\n4. added `tests/models/quantization/test_mimo_v2_qkv_shard.py`: new CPU-only unit test. It builds GA, SWA and Pro checkpoints in the export's chunk layout with known fp32 weights and asserts, for TP = 1, 2, 4, 8, that every rank's dequantized rows match an independent reference; that tp_size == ckpt_tp returns the checkpoint chunk unchanged; and that reading the SWA scales as one slice per KV head is detectably wrong (relL2 > 5x tolerance). \r\n\r\nFor reference, #53242 fixes only the SWA symptom (global row map — exact for SWA, but it mis-scales 62.7% of GA rows and would mis-scale 81.4% of Pro's), and #46755 adds the TP > `num_kv_heads` case with per-KV-head scale arithmetic, which for V2.5's MTP tensors would compute `116 // 8 = 14` and break TP=4 spec decode that works today. \r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nNon-spec, the reported configuration (TP=4) and TP=8 + EP:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nvllm serve XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5 --trust-remote-code --generation-config vllm \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --max-model-len auto --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\r\n  --tool-call-parser mimo --enable-auto-tool-choice --reasoning-parser mimo\r\n\r\nvllm serve XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5 --trust-remote-code --generation-config vllm \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --max-model-len auto --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\\r\n  --enable-expert-parallel \\\r\n  --tool-call-parser mimo --enable-auto-tool-choice --reasoning-parser mimo\r\n```\r\n\r\nSpec decode (MTP), both TP sizes:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nvllm serve XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5 --trust-remote-code --generation-config vllm \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --max-model-len auto --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\r\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mimo_v2_mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":1}' \\\r\n  --tool-call-parser mimo --enable-auto-tool-choice --reasoning-parser mimo\r\n```\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nlm_eval --model local-chat-completions \\\r\n  --model_args model=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5,base_url=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions,num_concurrent=32,max_retries=10,max_length=32000,timeout=60000 \\\r\n  --gen_kwargs '{\"max_tokens\":16000,\"until\":[]}' --batch_size auto \\\r\n  --tasks gsm8k --num_fewshot 25 --apply_chat_template\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n| check | before | after |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `vllm serve ... --tensor-parallel-size 4` | crash at load | **Server started, with sensible output** |\r\n| TP=8 (w/wo EP) | `AssertionError: TP size must evenly split the number of KV heads` | **Server started, with sensible output** |\r\n| TP=4 + MTP spec (`num_speculative_tokens=1`) | crash at load | loads, draft acceptance **~95%** |\r\n| TP=8 + (w/wo) EP + MTP spec | crash at load | **loads, draft acceptance 20703/21660 = 95.6%** |\r\n| GSM8K (TP=2/4/8) | n/a (never loaded) | ** around 0.9704 flex / 0.9712 strict ± 0.005** |\r\n| real tensors at TP=4 (GA, SWA, MTP), relL2 vs independent reference | crash | **0.0000** (pure chunk); TP=1/2 ≤ 0.011; TP=8 GA 0.0000, SWA 0.008-0.011 |\r\n| TP=2 end-to-end | crash | *Server started, with sensible output** |\r\n| synthetic GA/SWA/Pro checkpoints, TP 1/2/4/8 | crash / assert | 0.026-0.028 (fp8 round-trip floor) |\r\n| old reading (`ckpt_tp = num_kv_heads`) on SWA | — | detectably wrong: relL2 1.05 |\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>","created_at":"2026-09-18T05:56:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T13:05:01Z","closed_at":"2026-09-19T13:05:01Z","merged_at":"2026-09-19T13:05:01Z","merge_commit_sha":"211e252d0b4f8429f9b15fc52bdfed07782c7f70","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"AndreasKaratzas","id":42451412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNDUxNDEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42451412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas","html_url":"https://github.com/AndreasKaratzas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreasKaratzas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"DarkLight1337","id":44970335,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTcwMzM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44970335?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkLight1337","html_url":"https://github.com/DarkLight1337","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkLight1337/followers","following_u